 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Grab a spot in the shade near the entrance. Tents in the middle get sun all day and are tough to cool down. That's a good choice. The tree gives you shade both morning and afternoon, and you can roll your tent wall open for breeze at night. Cutting off the dead bit will often awaken it. Give each branch a good Drinking bird every morning, and they usually perk up. The pit is great for camping, but it gets busy in the heat of the day. If you can, tent on the shaded side. Exactly. And avoid any you think might break in a wind. Pop up tents take a bit of effort to set up, but they' worth it in a good site.",
